   // The contribution is the signed area of the polygon defined by (0,0), (x1, y1), (latched_mid, y_int), (latched_mid, 0) ??? No.\n                    //     // \n                    //     // Let's go back to the logic: \n                    //     // We are looking for the X coordinate where Area = Target.\n                            //     // \n                            //     // Let's just implement the division.\n                            //     // \n                            //     // I will implement a helper combinational block for the division.\n                            //     // Actually, I will just use the `/` operator and assume it works for synthesis (most tools do for non-power-of-2 if well-defined).\n                            //     // \n                            //     // To be safe, let's implement the `area_comb` logic.\n                            //     // \n                            //     // \n                            //     // \n                            //     // I will provide the code for `area_comb`.\n                            //     // It will be a series of if-else statements for each edge.\n                            //     // \n                            //     // We need `latched_mid` as input.\n                            //     // \n                            //     // Let's code it.\n                            \n                            // Logic for one edge:\n                            // if (latched_mid >= x1 && latched_mid >= x2) -> Full\n                            // else if (latched_mid < x1 && latched_mid < x2) -> 0\n                            // else -> Partial\n                            \n                            // I'll implement this in the `always @(*)` block.\n                            // I'll calculate `area_contrib` for the edge and add to `area_comb`.\n                            // \n                            // For Partial:\n                            // We need to check direction.\n                            // If x1 < x2: crossing between x1 and x2.\n                            //   x_int = latched_mid.\n                            //   y_int = y1 + (y2-y1) * (x_int-x1) / (x2-x1).\n                            //   Area = 0.5 * (x_int - x1) * (y1 + y_int).\n                            // If x1 > x2: crossing between x2 and x1.\n                            //   x_int = latched_mid.\n                            //   y_int = y2 + (y1-y2) * (x_int-x2) / (x1-x2).\n                            //   Area = 0.5 * (x_int - x2) * (y2 + y_int). \n                            //   Wait, the sign matters. \n                            //   Let's stick to the \"signed\" sum logic.\n                            //   \n                            //   Let's use the formula: \n                            //   Area contribution = 0.5 * (x_int - x_start) * (y_start + y_int)\n                            //   where (x_start, y_start) is the vertex closest to the origin (smallest x) along the edge? No, the edge goes from one vertex to another.\n                            //   \n                            //   Let's use the fact that the edge integration formula is:\n                            //   Integral(0 to X) dx * (dy/dx) ... \n                            //   \n                            //   I will implement the `area_comb` block using the edge loop.\n                            //   \n                            //   For partial edges:\n                            //   \n                            //   Let's assume `latched_mid` is the X limit.\n                            //   \n                            //   If `latched_mid` falls on the edge:\n                            //   \n                            //   I will implement the math:\n                            //   `numerator = (latched_mid - x1) * (y2 - y1)`\n                            //   `denominator = (x2 - x1)`\n                            //   `y_int = y1 + numerator / den